                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Labyrinths of the World: Shattered Soul is a typical game which tries to be great and fails in its execution. \nThe theme is a common one of a meglomaniac wanting to rule the world and capturing your sister who is his assistant in his lab.  He has stolen her soul and scattered it into different worlds.  You do have to suspend belief, but it is well done.  Graphics are gorgeous and high standard, music was good and fitted into the game well.\nThe downside was the execution of the game.  The cut scenes were clunky and blurry and at times went black.  When anything went into your dossier, the notification stopped the game dead.  Very clunky controls.  In the bonus chapter, the map didn't tell you where action needed to be done.\nIt is a pity because if these mechanics had been running smoothly, the game would have been very high quality.  At this moment, it was very frustrating at times and ruined my enjoyment.  6.7/10\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1567926700,
